{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>As three months.</b> The greater part of the first and the greater part of the last, and the middle one whole (Niddah 38a). And the expression כְּמִשְׁלֹשׁ חֳדָשִׁים is like 'the tripling of the months,' as in ״וּמִשְׁלֹחַ מָנוֹת״ (Esther 9), ״מִשְׁלוֹחַ יָדָם״ (Isaiah 11); and so Onkelos renders: כִּתְלָתוּת יַרְחַיָּא." "<b>Pregnant through harlotry.</b> It is a noun — pregnant, like 'a pregnant woman,' and like בָּרָה כַּחַמָּה." "<b>And she shall be burned.</b> Ephraim said, citing Rabbi Meir, a difficulty: she was the daughter of Shem, who was a priest — therefore they judged her by burning."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:41.513877869Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}